dup_mmap local verification draft — not launch ready

Frozen source: linux-mm-dup-mmap at
9cf27ef36d1d58cb65bd866d9f046ed2e56b045a.
REVIEWED_LAUNCH_READY remains False. Root must review and explicitly enable
before invoking run.sh. Do not run alongside the active release matrix.

This prepares fresh, serial C then Rust builds in
linux-out/dup-mmap-verification-001/{c,rust}; no cache seeds or copied fixtures.
The build image is pinned to
sha256:c02eb3929889b3f0cc035d57a02c844e0c74c71d24fbda1311249faeb8257f63.
Each build container is limited to two CPUs, 5 GiB and four hours; each guest
uses KVM/q35, two CPUs, 512 MiB and a 180-second timeout. The shared matrix
flock, active-container check, exclusive output creation and owned CID cleanup
prevent overlapping or accidentally reused execution. Failures remain in place.

Preflight requires the exact clean commit. Launcher and source hashes are
recorded and rechecked. Each side must pass the literal ordered seven-case
inventory plus terminal success; diagnostics, missing/extra/duplicate cases,
wrong config, failed exits and changed binaries or inputs reject the run.
The pair differs only by RUSIX_DUP_MMAP_RUST and must share guest binaries,
source inputs, compiler/package identities and VM settings. Both sides retain
Rust task construction, MM construction, release and copy implementations.

Postchecks run in the same pinned image with LLVM 19, never host LLVM. They
validate the original saved fork.i and mmap.i preprocessing records against
actual source, object, config, compiler-command and output hashes before
creating separate exclusive reinspection directories. Actual archive/object/
linked-symbol proofs are regenerated there. Only input_sha256 and
archive_member_sha256 path keys are remapped, recursively for the nested
mm_copy_selection proof, and only between the exact source/output mounts.
Original build evidence is not rewritten. All other proof fields remain exact.

Case order:
  shared_clone_write_and_exit
  shared_clone_exec_detaches_mm
  private_fork_cow
  dontfork_omits_only_advised_range
  wipeonfork_clears_child_and_grandchild
  private_file_mapping_cow_and_lifetime
  shared_file_mapping_survives_parent_unmap

Parent-reported static fixture compilation and its independent audit are prior,
separate evidence. This draft has not built or booted any kernel. Even a future
passing matrix establishes these seven ordinary consumers and selected code,
not allocation-failure rollback coverage, vm_ops->open coverage, leak freedom
or full MM compatibility. Runtime partial-allocation failure remains required
separate work. No host guest-binary execution is permitted.

After review and explicit enablement, root may run:
  bash linux-out/dup-mmap-verification-draft/run.sh
Do not invoke check-results.py manually on live/incomplete output. Its pinned
postchecks intentionally refuse reused evidence directories.
